course: dictionary
lesson: 13483
title: Identified
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To identify something means to recognise it, or to work out and name what it is. «We identified the bird from its song» means we knew which bird it was just by hearing it.
explain: You can also identify a problem. «She identified the problem» means she found out what was wrong and said it clearly. In science, you identify the variables in a test, which means you name the things that change.
explain: Look at the words after identified to find its meaning. «I identified with the main character» uses identified with, which means you felt you understood how the character felt, as if you were a little like them.
fact: Identify means to recognise who or what something is, or to name what it is.
fact: «Identified» is the past form of identify: «The police identified the thief from the camera.»
fact: «Identified with» means you feel you understand how someone else feels.
fact: In maths, «identified the shape» means you named which shape it was.
exercise: «The police identified the thief from the camera.» What does identified mean here? | Gave the thief a prize | *Found out who the thief was | Lost the thief in the crowd | Ran away from the thief
exercise: In science, we «identified the variables» in our test. What did we do? | Drew a picture of the test tube | Ate the variables for lunch | *Named the things that change in the test | Made the test take longer
exercise: «I identified with the main character.» What does this mean? | I wrote the character's name on a list | I stopped reading the book | I told the main character to go home | *I felt I understood how the character felt
test: «She identified the problem in the maths sum.» What did she do? | She hid the paper under her desk | She solved the sum and forgot it | *She worked out and named what was wrong
test: Which word is the past form of identify? | identify | identifies | identifying | *identified
exam: «The camera identified the car from its number plate.» What does identified mean? | Painted the car red | Stopped the car at the lights | *Recognised which car it was | Forgot about the car
